            <ArticleTitle>Antinociceptive activity of Ceriops decandra leaf and pneumatophore.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>261-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The ethanol extract of Ceriops decandra leaf and pneumatophore, at the oral doses of 250 and 500 mg/kg, showed a dose-dependent and significant inhibition of acetic acid-induced writhing in mice. On the contrary, the bark extract was devoid of any significant activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
